        "answer": {
          "short": "A straight line through the origin with gradient $15$, passing through $(1,15)$, $(\\frac12,7.5)$, $(\\frac13,5)$, $(\\frac14,3.75)$ and $(\\frac15,3)$.",
          "worked": "The corresponding horizontal coordinates are $1$, $\\frac12$, $\\frac13$, $\\frac14$ and $\\frac15$. Plot each against its corresponding $b$ value. The points lie on a straight line through the origin with gradient $15$.",
