      {
        "id": "p10-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Assuming that there is a simple relationship between the two variables, find a formula for $b$ in terms of $a$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$b=\\frac{15}{a}$",
          "worked": "The graph of $b$ against $\\frac1a$ is a straight line through the origin, so $b$ is inversely proportional to $a$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}b&=\\frac{k}{a}\\\\k&=ab\\\\k&=1\\times15\\\\k&=15\\\\b&=\\frac{15}{a}\\end{align*}$$\n\nEach other pair also gives $ab=15$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
